===================================

Running emberx without a build. Where each step stands after the cleanup PR:

1. Done: no build for development. In the repo each package's exports point at its src/, which every tool
   resolves as it is, imports from node_modules included, so @memserver/model's import of @emberx/string needed
   no bridge. The build gives each dist/ a package.json of its own, and that is what is published and packed.
   `npm test`, `build:dev` and `make build-dev` lost their build; CI's test jobs run with no dist/, so needing
   one again fails there.
2. Unchanged: @memoria/* replaces @memserver/* (its own PR). Nothing here waits on it any more.
3. Done: only TypeScript node can strip (erasableSyntaxOnly, verbatimModuleSyntax).
4. Done: emberx's decorators are standard ones (`@tracked accessor count = 0`), which Deno runs as they are, so
   `npm run test:deno` is `deno test` and `npm run test:doctests` is `deno test --doc`. Found on the way:
   qunitx's Deno build loads QUnit twice (dist/deno/index.js inlines it, and imports ../shared/assert.js, which
   imports vendor/qunit.js again); with a DOM present the second copy throws "QUnit has already been defined".
   test/setup-dom.js imports qunitx before it makes the DOM; worth fixing in qunitx itself.
5. Done: scripts/register.ts. `npm run test:node` runs test/node.ts as it is.
6. No compile step at all (long term, not ours alone): once JS engines run decorators (node 26 does not, even
   behind V8's --js-decorators), register.ts goes.
   Browsers always need .ts compiled, which qunitx and the dev server already do in memory, with no dist/.

Fewer scripts, as in qunitx (scripts/ there: check-benchmarks.ts, check-coverage.ts, release-consumer-test.ts,
sync-jsr-version.ts, test-release.sh). Each script is one more file a newcomer has to read, so a bare command
replaces it wherever one can:
- Same as qunitx, kept: check-benchmarks.ts, release-consumer-test.ts, test-release.sh.
- scripts/clean.ts: done, now `rm -rf` in package.json, as qunitx's build:cold.
- test-node.ts: done, gone: `npm run test:node` is a bare node command (step 5).
- lib/test-bundle.js, test-deno.ts, test-doctests.ts: done, gone: `deno test` and `deno test --doc`, as in
  qunitx (step 4); the doctests' `// =>` comments are explicit `assert.equal(...)` calls.
- dev.ts: done, gone: `npm run dev` is one esbuild command (--serve, --serve-fallback=public/index.html),
  now that nothing needs a plugin: Ember's modules come from @emberx/vendor, and exports point at src/.
- build-emberx-vendor.ts: new, writes @emberx/vendor from pinned devDependencies; register.ts: new, node's loader (step 5).
- release.ts: kept, renamed publish-emberx-packages.ts to say what it does. `npm version --workspaces
  --include-workspace-root` bumps all seven package.json files but leaves the exact @emberx/* dependency pins at
  the old version (checked with npm 11.19), and the packages must be published leaf-first.
- Now: build-emberx-vendor.ts, check-benchmarks.ts, publish-emberx-packages.ts, register.ts,
  release-consumer-test.ts and test-release.sh, plus lib/chrome-bench.js.
